\subsection{Automated Theorem Prover Layer}

Let $\mathcal{T}: \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{S}$ denote a state transition
in the hybrid dynamical system.  
The ATP constructs a formal derivation $\Pi$ such that:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{ATP}}(\Pi, \psi) = 1,
\end{equation}

where $\psi$ is the public proposition and $\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{ATP}}$
is the kernel-level verification predicate.  
All inference steps are checked against foundational axioms, eliminating
human heuristic bias.

\subsection{Zero-Knowledge Proof Layer}

The verified proof $\Pi$ is encoded into a succinct non-interactive
argument of knowledge (SNARK).  
Let $\kappa$ denote the security parameter.  
The soundness error satisfies:

\begin{equation}
\epsilon_{\mathrm{ZKP}} \leq 2^{-\kappa},
\end{equation}

ensuring that the probability of accepting an incorrect proof is
cryptographically negligible.

The ZKP layer guarantees:

\begin{itemize}
    \item proof correctness without revealing internal simulation data,
    \item verifier independence from the underlying state vector,
    \item composability with external validation systems.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Codex Provenance Anchor}

The SNARK output is committed to an immutable Codex registry via:

\begin{equation}
H_{\mathrm{commit}} = \mathrm{SHA256}(\Pi_{\mathrm{SNARK}} \parallel t),
\end{equation}

where $t$ is the timestamp and designer attribution.  
This establishes permanent provenance and prevents retroactive
modification.

\subsection{Lyapunov Stability Integration}

The hybrid organism engine provides a continuous stability envelope
through the Lyapunov functional $\mathcal{V}(X)$:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}(X) \leq 0
\quad \Rightarrow \quad
\text{No drift, contradiction, or divergence}.
\end{equation}

Any logical contradiction or unstable drift in the proof state triggers:

\begin{equation}
\dot{\mathcal{V}}(X) > 0
\quad \Rightarrow \quad
\text{Immediate rejection of proof state}.
\end{equation}

Thus, dynamical instability becomes a formal contradiction detector.

\subsection{Unified Irrefutability Criterion}

A proof $\Pi$ achieves ``beyond doubt'' status when:

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{ATP}}(\Pi, \psi) = 1,
\qquad
\epsilon_{\mathrm{ZKP}} \leq 2^{-\kappa},
\qquad
\mathcal{V}(X) \leq 0,
\end{equation}

and the Codex commitment is finalized.  
This yields a verification stack with:

\begin{itemize}
    \item formal logical certainty,
    \item cryptographic certainty,
    \item dynamical-system stability certainty,
    \item immutable provenance certainty.
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}

The Proof Validation Pipeline (PVP) establishes a mathematically and
cryptographically irrefutable verification architecture.  
By integrating theorem proving, zero-knowledge proofs, and Lyapunov
stability, the system achieves absolute proof validation beyond the
shadow of a doubt.